**Section 4: The Aha Moment (That Wasn't Instant)**

On Monday morning — day three — I finally did what I should have done on Friday: I took a heap snapshot of the live process using `--inspect` and pulled it into Chrome DevTools.

The summary view was overwhelming. The top of the retained-size list was dominated by `(string)` and `ArrayBuffer` entries. Millions of bytes of them. My first thought was that we were somehow buffering response data, or that the payload parser theory had been right all along.

