I switched to the "Containment" view and started walking the retainer chain. Each string was retained by an `IncomingMessage` object. Each `IncomingMessage` was retained by a `Map` entry. And every single one of those `Map` entries traced back to the same object — a `Map` sitting in module scope in `webhookHandler.js`.

I opened the file. And there it was.

```js
const idempotencyCache = new Map();

app.post('/webhook', (req, res) => {
  const eventId = req.headers['x-event-id'];
  if (idempotencyCache.has(eventId)) {
    return res.status(200).send('duplicate');
